%% UC-20 — Manage questionnaires
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor R as Researcher / Admin
    participant AP as Admin Panel
    participant B as Backend (questionnairesRouter)
    participant M as MongoDB

    R->>AP: Open Questionnaires page
    AP->>B: GET /api/v1/questionnaires
    B->>M: find(questionnaires)
    B-->>AP: definitions {slug, title, questions, scope}
    R->>AP: Create / edit questionnaire (question types, order, validation, scope: study|habit|donation)
    AP->>B: POST or PUT /api/v1/questionnaires/:id
    B->>B: Validate question schema
    B->>M: upsert(questionnaires)
    B-->>AP: 200
    R->>AP: Assign questionnaire to study (Study > Questionnaires tab)
    AP->>B: POST/PUT /api/v1/admin/studies/:id/questionnaire-assignments
    B->>M: upsert(questionnaire_assignments) + regenerate windows
    B-->>AP: 200

    Note over AP,M: SRHI is the one exception: it's unconditional (no library entry, no<br/>assignment — see intentionsRouter.js) and never appears in this tab. Any<br/>OTHER scope:'habit' questionnaire an admin defines behaves normally here —<br/>assignable/toggleable exactly like a study-scoped one, but its windows anchor<br/>to each participant's habit creation instead of enrollment (see UC-35), and<br/>it's invisible to a participant (Profile / Share tab, UC-06) until they've<br/>actually created a relevant habit.
    Note over AP,M: scope:'donation' is never assigned via the step above at all — it's<br/>selected directly as a study/group's post-donation questionnaire in<br/>Studies → Behavior Change (UC-36), and offered ad-hoc right after a<br/>habit donation (UC-03), bypassing the assignment/window system entirely.
